-- title:
--   The $n$-qubit Clifford group $\langle \mathrm{Had}, S, \mathrm{CNOT}\rangle$
-- statement:
--   The **Clifford group** on $n$ qubits is the subgroup of the unitary group generated by the Hadamard gate $\mathrm{Had}=\tfrac1{\sqrt2}\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\1&-1\end{pmatrix}$ and the phase gate $S=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&i\end{pmatrix}$ on each qubit, and the controlled-$X$ gate on each ordered pair of distinct qubits. It is finite, normalizes the Pauli group, and acts on labels by $\mathrm{Sp}(2n,\mathbb F_2)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The gates are the shared `QAlgorithms.hadamard`, `QAlgorithms.phaseS`, `QAlgorithms.cnot`, placed on wires by `QAlgorithms.embedOp` (identity elsewhere).
-- source:
--   Arunachalam, Schatzki, Optimal stabilizer testing and learning with limited quantum memory, arXiv:2607.02444 (version of 2 Nov 2026), §2.1, Cliffords and stabilizers, p. 14

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_Circuit

namespace StabTestMem

open QAlgorithms

/-- **The `n`-qubit Clifford group.** Arunachalam, Schatzki, *Optimal stabilizer testing and learning with limited quantum memory*, arXiv:2607.02444 (version of 2 Nov 2026), §2.1, "Cliffords and stabilizers", p. 14: "Clifford
unitaries are those generated by Hadamard gate Had = (1/√2) [[1, 1], [1, −1]], controlled-X gate
and S = [[1, 0], [0, i]] gate."

The subgroup of the unitary group of `n` qubits generated by the Hadamard gate and the `S` gate
on each wire and the CNOT gate on each ordered pair of distinct wires (control first).

**Formalization Note.** The gates are the shared `QAlgorithms.hadamard`, `QAlgorithms.phaseS`
(= `diag(1, i)`) and `QAlgorithms.cnot` (`|c, t⟩ ↦ |c, t ⊕ c⟩`), placed on the wires by
`QAlgorithms.embedOp` (identity on the other wires); an embedding `Fin 1 ↪ Fin n` is a wire, an
embedding `Fin 2 ↪ Fin n` an ordered pair of distinct wires (control, target). The generated group
is finite (all entries lie in `ℤ[e^{iπ/4}, 1/√2]` with bounded norm; global phases are powers of
`e^{iπ/4}`). -/
def cliffordGroup (n : ℕ) : Subgroup (Matrix.unitaryGroup (Qubits n) ℂ) :=
  Subgroup.closure
    {U | (∃ w : Fin 1 ↪ Fin n,
          (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) =
              embedOp (hadamard.submatrix (fun b => b 0) (fun b => b 0)) w ∨
            (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) =
              embedOp (phaseS.submatrix (fun b => b 0) (fun b => b 0)) w) ∨
      ∃ w : Fin 2 ↪ Fin n,
        (U : Matrix (Qubits n) (Qubits n) ℂ) =
          embedOp (cnot.submatrix (fun b => (b 0, b 1)) (fun b => (b 0, b 1))) w}

end StabTestMem


